--- math — numeric utility functions for the handl runtime.
---
--- Single source of truth for the `math` stdlib interface: 54 functions
--- covering arithmetic, constants, exponential/logarithmic, rounding,
--- trigonometry, and predicates. The Rust bridge in `plugin-lib-utils`
--- loads this file via `include_str!`, parses the `cap` declarations for
--- the plugin capability surface, and registers the Rust handls (handlers)
--- in an `OpRegistry` that dispatches each `op` to its native `f64` impl.
---
--- All 54 functions are FFI atoms (they call `f64` methods or Rust
--- arithmetic that cannot be expressed as pure handl arrows without
--- losing the exact `TypeMismatch` error messages the tests rely on).
--- The `op`/`handl` declaration form (ADR-0077 Phase 2) declares the
--- interface; the Rust `Function` impls in `ops.rs` provide the logic.
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- math.abs — absolute value of a number.
--- math.add — add two numbers.
--- math.ceil — ceiling of a number.
--- math.clamp — clamp a number between a lower and upper bound.
--- math.cos — cosine of a number (radians).
--- math.cosh — hyperbolic cosine of a number.
--- math.cbrt — cube root of a number.
--- math.asin — arc sine of a number.
--- math.acos — arc cosine of a number.
--- math.atan — arc tangent of a number.
--- math.atan2 — arc tangent of y/x using signs of both arguments.
--- math.asinh — inverse hyperbolic sine.
--- math.acosh — inverse hyperbolic cosine.
--- math.atanh — inverse hyperbolic tangent.
--- math.degrees — convert radians to degrees.
--- math.div — divide two numbers.
--- math.e — Euler's number (e).
--- math.exp — exponential function e^x.
--- math.factorial — factorial of a non-negative integer.
--- math.floor — floor of a number.
--- math.floor_div — integer (floored) division.
--- math.fract — fractional part of a number.
--- math.gcd — greatest common divisor of two integers.
--- math.hypot — hypotenuse: sqrt(a^2 + b^2).
--- math.infinity — positive infinity constant.
--- math.is_finite — test whether a number is finite.
--- math.is_infinite — test whether a number is infinite.
--- math.is_integer — test whether a number is an integer.
--- math.is_nan — test whether a number is NaN.
--- math.lcm — least common multiple of two integers.
--- math.lerp — linear interpolation between two values.
--- math.log — natural logarithm of a number.
--- math.log10 — base-10 logarithm of a number.
--- math.log2 — base-2 logarithm of a number.
--- math.map_range — map a value from one range to another.
--- math.max — maximum of two numbers.
--- math.min — minimum of two numbers.
--- math.mod — modulo of two numbers.
--- math.mul — multiply two numbers.
--- math.nan — NaN constant.
--- math.pi — pi constant.
--- math.pow — raise a number to a power.
--- math.radians — convert degrees to radians.
--- math.round — round a number to the nearest integer.
--- math.round_to — round a number to a given precision.
--- math.sign — sign of a number (-1, 0, or 1).
--- math.sin — sine of a number (radians).
--- math.sinh — hyperbolic sine of a number.
--- math.sqrt — square root of a number.
--- math.sub — subtract two numbers.
--- math.tan — tangent of a number (radians).
--- math.tanh — hyperbolic tangent of a number.
--- math.tau — tau (2*pi) constant.
--- math.trunc — truncate a number toward zero.
